1. the full form, no exception
   try body runs
   try body finished
   else runs: no exception was raised
   finally runs
2. the full form, an exception
   try body runs
   except runs: ZeroDivisionError
   finally runs
3. except (A, B) as e catches either class, and their subclasses
   caught ZeroDivisionError, isinstance(e, LookupError): False
   caught LookupError, isinstance(e, LookupError): True
   caught KeyError, isinstance(e, LookupError): True
4. no retry keyword: a loop around the try
   attempt 1
   attempt 2
   attempt 3
   succeeded on attempt 3
5. finally runs on return
   finally ran on the way out
   function returned 'the return value'
6. return inside finally swallows the exception (never do this)
   not run here: it swallows the same way, and Python 3.14 warns at compile time
7. no def-level except: the try is written out
   parse("12")  -> 12
   parse("abc") -> 'rescued ValueError'
8. what the caught object carries
   type(e).__name__   ZeroDivisionError
   str(e)             a str (CPython rewords messages; not printed)
   e.__traceback__    a traceback object
   extract_tb(...)    a StackSummary (paths inside, not printed)
9. try is a statement, not an expression
   v = try: ...  ->  SyntaxError
   (no else/ensure value to read: the block has no value at all)
